"Mild" conducts (like veganism), as you say, don't make the game much
harder, but they do require extra care (not to eat corpses, etc.).  The
challenge becomes winning Nethack *and* dealing with food shortages and
finding other ways to gain intrinsics.

There's quite a logic jump from there to this phrase, though:

>...I don't think that
> most conducts, even those that are kept track of by the game really are a
> measure of skill.

Atheist conduct, for example, requires resourcefulness to replace normal
b/u/c IDing on an altar, getting a good (or any) artifact weapon, uncursing
and blessing stuff.

Illterate conduct means you have to figure out what stuff is *without* ?id,
can't enchant your armor or weapon, etc.

These are not the hardest conducts and IMO they each require more Nethack
skill and knowledge to ascend than does a non-conduct game of vanilla.
Combining those two conducts requires even more skill, IMO and the really
hard conducts and combos thereof require even more so.

